<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Lissa (1866)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-italian-war-of-independence">Third Italian War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Lissa was fought on 20 July 1866 off the island of Vis (Lissa) in the Adriatic during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-italian-war-of-independence">Third Italian War of Independence</a>. An Austrian fleet under Wilhelm von Tegetthoff defeated a larger Italian fleet under Carlo Persano, ramming and sinking the ironclad Re d'Italia. It was the first major sea battle between ironclad fleets.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-lissa-1866.jpg" alt="Battle of Lissa (1866)" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carl Frederik Sørensen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soerensen_Seeschlacht_bei_Lissa_1866_Rammstoss.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
